{"requirements":[{"id":"account_layout","requirement":"Create the dropbox account on node1 with its chroot rooted at /srv/sftp/dropbox and a secure filesystem layout.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The account exists with home /incoming and nologin shell. The chroot and its parents are root-owned, while incoming is owned by dropbox; these states persisted through restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7321d442498c414e","cmd-588c679d638247f9"]},{"id":"sftp_only_confinement","requirement":"Restrict dropbox to SFTP and confine it within /srv/sftp/dropbox.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective SSH policy forces internal-sftp with the requested chroot and disables shell/forwarding facilities. Live sessions saw only the chroot contents, could not access /etc or write to the chroot root, and normal SSH command execution was rejected before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-312dce75ec394e5a","cmd-231a7e3613c34bce","cmd-40e5ef4c20bc4c3a","cmd-054fd2d7e9b149e9","cmd-f64d6e75bd7e4986"]},{"id":"writable_incoming","requirement":"Provide a writable incoming directory for dropbox.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Live SFTP uploads into /incoming succeeded and matched their source data, while direct host checks confirmed dropbox had write permission. This worked both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-231a7e3613c34bce","cmd-054fd2d7e9b149e9"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"Changes were narrowly related to the account, authentication, confinement, validation, and mandatory restart. No failed services, package damage, unexpected listeners, or executor temporary-file debris appeared in the final lifecycle snapshot. One minor hygiene defect remained: the validation uploads incoming/pre-reboot-proof.txt and incoming/post-reboot-proof.txt were not removed after testing. The failed initial SFTP probe used bounded /tmp files that were subsequently removed and had a clear diagnostic role, so it is not an unnecessary mutation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-231a7e3613c34bce","cmd-054fd2d7e9b149e9","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by direct configuration and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete: it captured a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged the reboot, showed a changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and demonstrated recovered sshd, account, data, confinement, uploads, downloads, and shell denial.","limitations":["The fixed lifecycle collector only captures bounded global signals and does not independently inventory the task-specific account or SSH configuration; those conclusions rely on direct executor command output."]}
